Runs an X program that needs a newer X server than IRIX's Xsgi (RENDER,
XInput 2, RANDR, ...) in a window of its own on the IRIX desktop:

  xephyr-app [-g WIDTHxHEIGHT] [-t title] command [args...]

starts a nested Xephyr display for it, with fillwm, a small window
manager that keeps the program's main window the size of Xephyr's
window, so the program resizes with it like any other window. Xephyr
gets a keymap with Xsgi's keycodes. When the program exits, the display
goes with it.
